note Pairs lines unique to both sides first, then grows pairs into equal neighbours and recurses into the gaps. Growth starts only from a pair, so an open edge never pairs a slice's closing brace with the end of a longer function; the paired flags say whether the line just before and the line just after a gap are paired. Lines compare with surrounding whitespace trimmed, so re-indented code still pairs.

